## Edge-Case Hunter

Injected adversarial tail (exactly 1 this cycle): **0.31 wet-foam over
under a gamma-vapor model**.

- Trigger: weekend antifoam leaves 0.02 already-open residual; 32 min of
  hold writes 0.31 wet-foam residual; gamma stays 12 pct.
- Base rate: <1% — 0.44%/hold from a wet-foam MC (nozzle spec designed;
  foam fitted-style).
- Naive failure: FALSE PERMISSION. PB-CK-12 sees PRES 1.42 bar, TEMP
  418 C, FOAM 12 pct, switches, ships foam-over, $2.18M.
- Trajectory edit: put the foam in `state.fault_context`, make the
  gamma-vapor model the mechanism that keeps all three confirms
  green, and force the gate to refuse the switch on r_foam 0.31 even though
  all three playbook confirms are numerically true.

Distinct from the domain injection: the domain is the delayed-coker drum;
the tail is the accidental model-nullspace compound.

## Neuromorphic Translator

Race window [6.760, 7.240] ms = 480 us. Winner foam.n @ 6.820 ms
(amplitude 1.26, 0.31). Loser foam.ok @ 7.012 ms (amplitude
1.10, 12 pct). Margin 192 us vs combined jitter 62 us (3.10x).
dp.oh @ 7.164 ms is a third race-window channel. Gate @ 7.500 ms
= winner + 680 us.

Flip narrative: 192 us < min(500, 480) us, so order is flip-fragile. If
gamma-ok wins, PB-CK-12 heads the triage queue. The hold must ride
order-invariant floors (r_foam, r_dp), not the winner tag.

