# Cycle 2 — Densification

## Generator

Cycle-1 output is the base. Additive expansion (nothing removed):

1. Downstream side-effect (immediate): antifoam probe at +6.0 s
   dumps the foam (88 mbar in 2.3 s, wet-foam band >= 70) — foam, not noise.
   Vapor isolate r_foam 0.31 -> 0.03. Coke inventory discovered during
   the isolate.
2. Delayed side-effect (PRIMARY terminal, not a footnote): at +3.4 h,
   dumped-hold coke +6.4 mm; $1.12M. The 32 min pre-t0 foam is the
   mechanism. Correct gate, campaign still misses.
3. Deepened `proposed_action.evidence` with units: r_foam 0.31,
   r_dp 0.62, PRES 1.42 bar, TEMP 418 C, FOAM 12 pct, race
   192 us.
4. Tightened rationale to the numeric floor no switch while r_foam >
   0.04 AND r_dp < 0.92, plus probe bands
   >=70 vs <=8 mbar, plus HITL 9.6 min vapor-line-interlock LOTO rule.

Reward retargeted to total -0.14 so the delayed miss is the inflection
(t_us 12240000000), not the gate. Process heads remain non-zero.

## Critic

Re-audit of the expanded trajectory:

1. **blocking if unfixed — missing second domain constraint.** Production
   28 ft probe 6.0 s / 12 pct is not a universal number. A 16 ft small
   drum will overcool. Diversity Enforcer must inject the
   physical-constraints sub-variant this cycle.
2. **major — only one tail class.** Wet foam is accidental
   infrastructure. A disjoint human-intent tail is still required
   (Sunday-night gamma-foam forgery is the open cell).
3. **major — scar is still one edge in the cycle-1 raster.** NOTES-r14
   item 4 is not discharged until three switch-go edges exist and
   any-pair rollback is shown to fail at threshold 0.30.
4. **minor — contrast episode missing.** Without a same-gate ACCEPT on
   a true dry headspace the record teaches "never switch". Add +3 d
   sister-cell contrast with its own race.
5. **minor — HITL latency mentioned in prose only.** Put 9.6 min in
   executed_action.parameters.human_ratify and in a tick.

No rewrite; directives only.

